From 7f4c35359e657187ea63b76d65e6f29d844f164c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:28:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a block on David must say what unblock and
 archive mean in its ask line [daveey]

kanban_block and kanban_create (tool entry points) refuse a human_request whose
action does not state what unblocking and what archiving the card do
(rejection user_ask_incomplete). The action is the line David sees verbatim on
the card and in chat close-out notices; asks like 'Pick A, B or C' left him
reading 'blocked' with nothing to act on (coach pattern
blocked-card-missing-user-ask). Internal trackers (kb.create_task) are not
linted. The lint runs after the standing-wait and park guards so their
refusals keep precedence.

Tests: tests/tools/test_kanban_user_ask_lint.py (3 fail before, 4 pass after);
fixtures with ask-less actions updated.
